APPLE IIGSIMAGEWRITER DRIVERTESTINGCURRENT AND PREVIOUS RELEASE NOTESBEN KONING-----For easiest testing on the system disk, rename the file"ImageWriter.Dxx" to "ImageWriter" while transferring from theMacintosh to the Apple IIGS into the */SYSTEM/DRIVERS directory.  Thisway you don't have to modify the "AT ImageWriter" CDEV.The PRINTER and MODEM port drivers had a bug which caused the LQ driverto print garbage on certain occasions (when $89 or $09 sent to portdriver by printer driver).  Please install the new versions in theDRIVERS directory.The PRINTER and MODEM have also been modified to support true 19.2Kbaud output rate for the ImageWriter LQ.The PRINTER and MODEM port drivers have been modified so thatresponse is much quicker if the printer was unconnected or inrecognizing that an ImageWriter I is connected.-----System Disk 6.0 ships here.F38		8-Jan-92Removed WaitCursor/InitCursor calls from status message routines.  Most applicationsput up their own (wait) cursors anyway, and our WaitCursor call was causing problemswith applications such as HyperCard which do cursor animation with hi-bit-setcursor record pointers.F37		10-Dec-91Paper sizes for International A4 and International Fanfold changed as per customerrequest: X size increased from 132 to 136 80-dpi-pixels.  Untested.F36		4-Dec-91Dialog box radio buttons hit area now set to 0,0 so it's computed by toolbox.F35		15-Nov-91Dialog box tabbing for PrJobDialog works to all three LineEdit boxes.F34		23-Aug-91Printer soft reset command now includes setting the language to American.  Fixesbug in text mode where our-nonmapped iw-mappable characters ("#", etc) would beerroneously mapped if the DIP switches were set for any language other than American(WE map everything and want the iw to not do any mapping of its own!).Now storing zeros in our-picframe X1 and Y1 before we allow the user-supplied rect(if any) to be copied in.  Retrofix bug fix from SW driver.F33		20-Jun-91Saying "Rendering page image" again; Bob doesn't like "Rasterizing".  Geez!F32		19-Jun-91Cosmetic: changed LineEdit box bounding rectangles and say "Rasterizing page image".Added wDev bit 15: If set (by app), then during-printing status box is not shown.F31		13-Apr-91Got rid of commented-out stuff in spool.aii source file.Incremented version number to 4.2.Job dialog box no longer updates twice when first drawn.  Style dialog stillredraws twice because of its funky portrait/landcape controls.Command-Period works (as well as ESC) as key-equivalent for Cancel inboth Setup and Job dialog boxes.Saved code space by converting NotCorrectDevDialog to AlertWindow usage.Saved code space by converting CheckAndDoAboutBox to AlertWindow usage; addedBob Haven's name to about box.Saved code space by using WaitUntil in ShowPrinterErrorStatus routine.System Disk 5.0.4 ships here.F30		2-Dec-90 6pmThe printer communication error (IW) and resending of imager-call-band (LQ)is happening when it shouldn't.  Probably bug in appletalk PAP code; "fixed"by calling PrDevStatus (PAPStatus) a second time if a tool error occurred.In other words, PAPStatus, is returning an error ($805-Name Not Found) andwhen it's called immediately after, it returns no error.F29		30-Nov-90 5:30pmModification to end of CloseDoc code to ensure that the SpoolFinishGET isalways called if there is a print loop error, to ensure that spool memory orfiles are deallocated/removed (note that unique printer connection is not anissue here since the printer connection open/close is all in PicFile).F28		29-Nov-90 7pmTJ089 bug found by Mensch/Dave.  AppleShare interaction, messing with QDdirect page.  Was going to work around this problem by doing save/restorearound all OS calls; but found that it wasn't effective enough.  Thusappleshare FST is now being revved to save/restore QD around its calls toShieldCursor.  The routines to work around this problem have been left andcommented out.F27		28-Nov-90 2:15pmSpoolPut code now works; lost sync bug still exists.F26		27-Nov-90The TJ089 bug still exists.  Lost sync, presumably during SpoolPut.Added code to SpoolPut: when it is opening a file to spool to becausememory is running low, we check to see if we booted over a network,and if so, we try to write the temporary file into the correct entryof the USERS directory; the same 'TMP.XXXX'-style file is created there.This needs to be tested thoroughly.The above changes in the spooler are to be cut-pasted directly from theIW driver to the LQ driver since the spoolers/entry points are identical;did "equal" anyway to check to make sure first.Near the "PutGetExit" code in printloop.aii, the exit accumulator/carryerror status was not always being set if there was an error returned fromSpoolGet (or SpoolPut, for that matter).  This was at first thought tocreate the above DrawPicture crashing bug, but this fix is good enough tobe left in anyway.F25		24-Nov-90Added space on either side of slash which divides the printer drivername and the port driver name at the top of both dialog boxes.Crashing bug was found to be bank-wrap-around problem in ROM 3 QDcursor handling code.F24		19-Nov-90We discovered that the latest crashing bug is caused by two things:1) QDaux has a problem with running out of memory during the DrawPictureprocess: it has an internal stack imbalance problem and crashes.  Thishas been fixed in 6.0.  We need to put in this change--only--for 5.0.4.2) In both the IW and in the LQ drivers, we were not checking fortool error after DrawPicture; now, upon any DrawPicture error, both thetool call error from PrPicFile and the print loop error (PrError) areset.F23		13-Nov-90Incremented version number from 4.0 to 4.1.In SpoolPut, there was no error checking on the SetHandleSize call (werelied on the RealFreeMem call just above)!  "BCS PutNoMoreMemory" addedjust after SetHandleSize (found by Mensch).Allowed Iduna to exit better when just starting PrPicFile; Iduna patchesout event manager so we need to rely on polling the PrError and we shouldbe executing the IdleProc to give Iduna the chance to set the PrError.We were doing this in the normal imaging routines but not from withinthe PrinterOpen routine in printloop.  Fixed: PrinterOpen now callsBufferIdleProc right at the very beginning and exits if PrintLoopError-Status is set; and PrPicFile now checks PrintLoopErrorStatus andallows exit right after its PrinterOpen call.5.0.3 System Disk is Golden Master and has shipped around 1-Nov-90.F22		13-Aug-90Text-mode font mapping now handles case where GetTextSize call returnsa zero.  Fixes "Nexus" applicaton quirk.B21		9-Aug-90Upon the PrDevWrite call, we don't treat $08FF as an error, because itcould be simply PAP saying that the printer's appletalk buffer is full.Retrofit from LQ's Iduna choking after several cards bug.  B20		7-Aug-90		For System Disk 5.0.3 D17 Final CandidateIduna and other apps which repeat the print loop were only able toprint the first page in color, because the self-ID for IW-I/II ischecked at each PrinterOpen internal call and if the printer is busythen we erroneously assume IW-I.  Fixed by only allowing the IW-I/IIflag to change--one way or the other--the first time PrinterOpenhappens.  The only way it will happen again is if we're reloaded.This works as long as the user does not use both an IW I and an IW IIduring the same sitting in the same application.Iduna draft printing didn't work anymore, due to a misguided "bug fix"in B16 to "fix" "nonworking" PaintWorks Gold problem.  PWG and Idunaboth work perfectly fine; it's just that PWG tries to print graphicsin Draft mode, which is supported by the old IW driver but not by thenew driver.  It was thus a big mistake to change GetQuality in B16.Fixed by making GetQuality once again responsive to the bjDocLoop field(negating the change in B16).  This makes Iduna but breaks PaintWorksGold (which doesn't work without a patch of 5.0+ systems anyway).  Thefundamental question is if we need to support graphics in Draft mode.B19		24-Jul-90The PrPixelMap call was not working correctly when connected to anImageWriter-One.  Problem showed up as leading 0's to the left of linesof print.  Fixed by making sure that CompressSend does not send colorribbon select commands if abIsIWOne actionbit is set.  Also, addedIW-One/Two check in the entry code for PrPicFile (done by a reentrantPrGetPrinterSpecs call).B18		19-Jul-90Imager is now able to monitor PrError during the actual process ofprinting.  Allows Iduna abort response to be much better.  This isdone herein only for non-draft and is implemented by giving the imagerour own idleproc which in turn calls the user idleproc.  The imager'sown abort flag--PrError--has been made an exported global to facilitatethis.  Should be retrofitted to LQ after raising confidence level.B17		18-Jul-90OpenDoc no longer saves individual values from the print recordthat are needed by OpenPage/ClosePage--it saves the value of the user'sprint record handle instead.  Fix for apps which modify rPage and otherfields between OpenDoc and OpenPage.  Impact on testing is on manualfeed, idleproc, number of copies, and page range correctness.B16		16-Jul-90Made the internal metrics GetQuality routine insensitive to the settingof the bjDocLoop field in the print record.  This field is normallyset to 0 if in text mode.  GetQuality thus gets that piece ofinformation exclusively from our new wQuality print record field.Fixes/works around a "bug" with PaintWorks Gold.B15		5-Jul-90Got rid of now-unused "s_dfl_lf" and "s_dfl_paplen" strings.ImageWriter-One carriage return speed: no change.  Tried going tounbold and lesser-resolution modes for either carriage return orline feed only; made no difference in timing tests.  Perhaps a characterneeds to be output for this to be effective, but even a cursory tryat that proved ineffective.OldIW compared to NewIW speed in Better+Color (has nothing to do withappletalk): no change.  It's a policy decision to turn boldface off ifin Better with color, but then things wouldn't look as nice with (orwithout) a less-than-brand-new ribbon.  Plus, for bitmapped drawingsthe (faster) Standard mode looks just as good or better.  Plus, we havethe Faster mode, which really rips.  My recommendation is to leave thecurrent boldface/no-boldface scheme as-is, even if that means thatnon-interlaced, better mode color images print somewhat slower.B14		28-Jun-90Added field to print record "wResScaling" at printX+20 ($78 absolute)offset in the print record.  The wResScaling is a constant whichdescribes how much this printer driver scales up the image (just priorto scaled-down printing at finer dot pitch) in order to obtain higherresolution.  This field has been added for the application's information.It always has a constant value of 2 for the ImageWriter.Job Dialog user interface line edit box fix:  Wherever the line editcursor is blinking, no matter in which of the 3 boxes, typing ispossible, even if a non-line edit control was just selected.  Fixed byremoving ParamWordA-flag restriction in ConductJobDialog; the LE handlethat is kept around is now always valid.B13		27-Jun-90Added lda #0 to pha's just before GetNetworkName in imager to be sure.Retrofit from LQ driver.The printer would not respond in many situations with a cut sheet feederattached.  We were setting default printer options in imager'sIWShutDown routine on the way out.  This caused problems with the sheetfeeder because those commands would be buffered up, and the printerwould then not respond to the next self-id, which could be immediatelyafter a PrJobDialog (preventing printing), or just before it (causingthe driver to erroneously assume IW-One).  Fixed.A12		27-Jun-90		on system disk 503d15Colors have been make to contain just a bit more magenta; makes theperiwinkleblue640 screen background color a bit purpler.If Better+Color+640+noninterlaced+nonnotunibo ("Fast"), then boldfaceis turned off during the black band print.  This is done in Portraitmode only, because Landscape is always interlacing in the Better modes.This makes 640 Better colors much less muddy.  Too bad it isn'tpossible to put this in LQ driver.Slight problem fixed in 640 black/white graytone assignment withlight yellow and periwinkle blue.PurgeAll/CompactMem have been taken out.  It can still gag applicationswith these two things installed.  Bufdims break taken out.  Still leftto do are more lowmem tests, sheet feeder, and final-breakers.A11		19-Jun-90This is a release for checking if all the imager modes all still workcorrectly and verify that color handling is better.The Text Mode text-recording-bottleproc now does not record a string ifits origin is outside of the current clipping region.  The current clipregion was set by OpenPage but may be modified by advanced applicationssuch as Iduna.  Fixes DrawPlus extra-line-of-text-on-second-page bugand similar Iduna bug.  Must be retrofitted to LQ driver.Previously, in 320-mode, KCMY values were doubled in density betweenbeing calculated from RGB and being stored in the linebuffer.  This madecolors look brighter but made Black/White printing horrible.  Now theKCMY values are doubled only if 320-mode AND color-mode.  King Tut,the girl on the bike, and other 320-mode scanned pictures look muchbetter.  Should be retrofitted to LQ driver.In PrOpenPage, we forgot to skip over the OpenPicture call and therelated spool-beginning code just above it if in Text/Draft mode.Therefore, spooling memory as well as a picture handle was createdinadvertently if in Draft/Text mode.  Fixed by adding some newbranching at end of OpenPage and at beginning of ClosePage code, as wellas change in order of first two things at beginning of CloseDoc code,so that dialog is removed *after* if-draft-PrinterClose code.  Must beretrofitted to LQ driver.Changed names of quality modes as follows: Text Only, Fast, Standard,and Best.  Should be retrofitted to LQ driver.The RGB to KMCY conversion formula has been changed slightly to rendercolors that are a little more red (for 640-periwinkle blue, forexample).The dither patterns have been painstakingly redone, yielding asmoother gray scale.320-mode color-density doubling in imager has been removed; it is nolonger necessary with the new dither patterns (in 160 hdpi mode).Black/White 640-mode handling has been changed to maintain correctnesseven upon encountering light yellow (which could not show up asanything otherwise).In all modes except Fast--even Standard--the horizontal resolution ofthe halftone dither density patterns is now 160 hdpi.  The singleexception to this rule is that in the case of Standard+640 mode+Color,the 80 hdpi mode is used anyway.  Results: better graphics patternswith fewer artifacts, no more juvenile-looking patterns in 340 mode,and more.  Disadvantages: there are still some artifacts in 640Black/White rendition of a color image, and doing this makes theStandard mode slower.  By the way, this is the way that the oldImageWriter does it.  Note that Fast still prints at 80hdpi, and notethat the patterns in Fast mode have actually become uglier--butwe don't care.  It is implemented as imager-qbit#14, set by GetConvert-QualBits if mode=Fast.  Thus now it is possible to have an object withjaggedy edges, effectively at 80 hdpi, while the pattern inside issmooth because its pixels are 160-hdpi-small.  Works for Portrait andLandscape.  All different Port/Land/640/320/VC/Reduction/Fast/Std/Bettmodes must be retested.If 640+standard+color, then the imager forces the (old) 80 hdpipatterns, since the 640-screen-dithering would otherwise make the colorsway too muddy.DIAGNOSTICS: PurgeAll/CompactMem is happening at beginning of OpenDocand end of PrPicFile.  This crashes AppleWorks GS.  Also, theSetBufDims breakpoint ($BD) is still in place.A10		30-May-90The PRINTER and MODEM port drivers have been modified so thatresponse is much quicker if the printer was unconnected or inrecognizing that an ImageWriter I is connected.Inside PrClosePage is the ClosePicture call.  If this call returns anerror, as it would if our bottleprocs failed (due to full disk, etc)during page data recording, that error is now returned out of thePrClosePage call as a tool error.  Must be retrofitted to LQ driver.The 8K RGB to KCMY conversion table is no longer used.  Instead, aconversion lookup table which is parallel in structure to the standard16-entry color table is used.  Only those color palettes which arereferenced by an SCB are calculated.  Results in practical eliminationof delay for calculating an entire 4096-entry lookup table, and about a7.4K reduction in memory footprint.  Everything on earth having to dowith standard or nonstandard color tables as well as the new colormodel PicComments needs retesting.  Could be retrofitted to LQ driver.Iduna's command-period abort was not working.  After the imagingroutine call, during which the IdleProc runs, we now check the printloop error (PrError/PrSetError) status.  It was already being doneat the beginning of each sheet; now it is done every after everyimager call.  AppleTalk error message handling needs retesting!Must be retrofitted to LQ driver.A9		23-May-90Fixed disk label sizes for 1/4" vert spacing b/w labels.Change-Color-Table and Change-Range-Of-SCB's PicComment operation hasbeen tested.It's been determined that crashing under HP/std/pict-window washappening due to too many DAs/INITs/etc taking up memory and the Loadercould not load a QDAux segment.  Therefore simply another example oflow-mem situation.Changed the RGB to KCMY conversion table-building routines to allowit to be a true handle, rather than a big DS.B segment.  The handle isactually unlocked when the imager is not active, thus allowing its 8K tobe moved around by the Memory Manager if necessary.  Also saves 8K-on-disk for FST's that don't handle sparse files (unlike ProDOS but likeHFS, for example).  In actual practice right now, the handle usuallyresides in another bank than the loaded driver, thus easing its foot-print in fragmented memory space.  Can be retrofitted to LQ driver asneeded.A much smaller direct-page stack frame is used for the GetPic/PutPicbottleprocs, as per suggestion by Mensch.  This may or may not have anyeffect on low-memory bugs, but makes for better coding practice.For next release, we may investigate a new spooler which breaks up theto-memory big movable block into many little separate movable blocks,making it easier to survive in a memory-fragmented system.D8		11-May-90		Alpha candidateText-mode bug fix: there was a word-store to "n_textfont", whichshould be a byte.Manual page feed crashing bug.  Selecting land+vc+bett+manual feed wouldcause crash.  Crash was in _NoteAlert, because in PrPicFile's setbufdimscode, we blindly set the number of horizontal bytes to our bandbufferlocinfo's number of scanline bytes.  During landscape printing, ourbandbuffer is very tall and skinny--a small number of horizontalscanline bytes, thus messing quickdraw functions other than our imagingup very badly.  Fixed by ensuring that PrPicFile's setbufdims code canonly make the qd bufdims bigger, and never smaller.  This would alsocause many other wierd printing problems in any landscape mode.Very slight modifications to text-mode font mapping; less overlap.We're now remembering the handle from the OpenPicture call in theOpenPage routine and passing it to KillPicture in the ClosePageroutine.  We were leaving one small handle per page around.  Must beretrofitted to LQ driver.Added new paper types: "3.5 Disk" label (2-3/4 x 2-3/4 inch) and "5.25 Disk" label (4-3/4 x 1-1/4 inch).  These pin-fed labels are onorder for testing.  Should be retrofitted to LQ driver.Discovered and fixed small dormant bug: near imager.aii/"next_intl",should insert AND #$FF after longm just before adding to "lang_tbl".Should be retrofitted to LQ driver.Symptom: TopDraw/50%/"US Statement"-paper-size/print lab machine #1wouldn't print all the way down the page (it wouldn't print all bands).Logic bug fixed in band buffer size allocation code.  "PiFiLastBand-Height" would be zero and *used* as last band's height when the papersize with metrics settings happened to be an even multiple of thecurrent band buffer size, given the current memory conditions.  Fixedby preinitializing PiFiLastBandHeight to the band buffer height andmodifying it only if there was a nonzero remainder from the divide call.In this way, PiFiLastBandHeight is always a true indicator of the lastband's tallness in all possible situations.  Must be retrotitted to LQdriver.Symptom: In PaintworksPlus, selecting Better would cause the driver toprint half too small and do a too-short formfeed.  The application istrying to force Standard mode in all cases; and thus even with the fixthe quality is still Standard.  Also, the fix should correct the partialformfeed problems which appear in same tests.  Fix is two changes inmetrics "GetQuality" routine: 1) AND #$FF instead of wrong longm/shortm,and 2) added code to force our internal quality rendition ("wQuality")to 2 (standard) if (old wQuality == 3) AND (wDev better bit == 0).  Thisfixes any temporal discrepancy between better/not-better status obtaineddirectly from wDev or by means of GetQuality call.  Must be retrofitted,in an appropriate way, to LQ driver, which only has 0..2 quality types.D7		1-May-90Some measures have been taken to do grafport handling more like the olddriver; this seems to alleviate some of the hanging problems.  NOTE:This release DOES NOT purport to be the final low-memory fix, it isa release intended to recieve feedback on this sticky problem.  Abreakpoint (BRK #$BD) has been left in on purpose (QD bufdims alloc).Removed PurgeAll/CompactMem at beginning of OpenPage.Fixed dialog layout of "Copies:" title item (moved it up a little).Removed paper sizes that are impossible on the ImageWriter from tableand popup menu (> 8.5" horizontal size).Interchanged paper types for European B5 and IntlFanFold.  TheIntlFanFold is now (correctly) type=3, European B5 is type=4.  Mustbe retrofitted to LQ driver.The spooler now uses RealFreeMem in the memory/disk decision code.Removed two cases of CheckHandle call in "entry.aii".Despite run-length-encoding, Appletalk printing is/was slow.  There is atremendous overhead for sending many short PAP write requests anddoing PAPStatus requests.  Therefore, by adding caching capability tothe "writeshort"/"writelong" routines, Appletalk printing speeds shouldimprove greatly.  Will simplify text-mode intl char routine; might beretrofitted to LQ.Made equates for both mix/max flow quantum (min ==> writeshort cachesize).Made alternate call entry point "IdleProcAbortCheck" which doesn't doPrDevStatus but does do the command-period/idleproc; this alternateentry point is used during the imaging loops.  Done because PrDevStatus/PAPStatus is very slow.  This means that the network error reportingtime granularity is greater (only at beginning near "goPrintPix").All the calls inside the banding loops, except at beginning/open/etccode have been changed to the quicker "IdleProcAbortCheck" insteadof "IdleProcAbortErrCheck".Text-mode international char caching removed because no longer necessarywith our generalized output caching (IW only).Text-mode bug fix: (imager/text output/cmp #$20 for ctrl-char can'twork; must do AND #$00FF to get rid of garbage in upper 8 bits of ACC).Must be retrofitted to LQ driver.Appletalk self-id is now always done using PrDevStatus.  It is morereliable and somewhat faster.  Affects code all over in "IWStartup"and "IWShutdown", adds case to "abDoImage" check, affects "PrinterOpen".Should be retrofitted to LQ driver.  Appletalk PrClosePage FREEZES atend of job with a sheet feeder, however!The above exposed a two nasty but simple text-mode bugs: near the codeto "select one of the printer's built-in text fonts/sizes" in theimager text-mode section no AND was being done on SCBListPtr+1 andSCBListPtr+0.  Very bad, because the former is used to index a lookuptable of writeshort-strings!D6		18-Apr-90I have determined that the long IW I ID delay also occurs in the oldIW driver (but it does it only once, right after head recalibration, soit doesn't appear to be as bad).  In order to fix this problem properlyfor the new drivers, the PRINTER and MODEM port drivers will have to bechanged; and the change required would be incompatible with the olddriver.  Also, a new speed improvement possiblity has been discussed(important for LQ).  Therefore, a skunk-works new-port-driver projectis underway.The portrait color vertical interlace code was printing the same datafor the 2nd pass interlace bands, because it was doing "restinfo" callsto rewind pointers to pre-"nextPline"-call data.  Fixed.  One visibleeffect of this, for example: In portrait+color+better+vc, the effectivevertical resolution on the paper would be half, compared to samesettings but with black/white.  Color patterns looked bad as well.Density dither patterns have been much improved; far fewer artifactsare exhibited."Allocating imaging memory" status message added.  Will be retrofittedto the LQ driver.The spooler now uses GS/OS class 1 calls so that it can cache duringpicture playback, resulting in fewer disk seeks.  Will be retrofittedto the LQ driver.Several changes have been made to address low-memory-during-DrawPicture(Memory potentiometers, RealFreeMem call, no more MaxBlock call, Set-BufDims value changes, Purge/Compact @ before OpenDoc time).  It seemsto work now--with a 1M ROM 03 with a 64K RAM disk and a LOT (~250K) ofCDA's and NDA's, running MultiScribe--MOST of the time.  It's stillpossible to make it perform poorly, by loading up the system with evenmore stuff; but such is also possible with the old driver.  Comparisontesting needs to be done.  Will be retrofitted to the LQ driver whenthe confidence level from all these changes rises.D5		11-Apr-90Changed "50% Vertical Size" string in dialog box to "VerticalCondense".  Which is better?Final source code cleanup; much documentation has been added.Landscape with 320-mode vertical interlace imaging scaling was wrong(2x too tall).  Fixed; now each 320-mode pixel counts for two pin fires.Landscape 320-mode color saturation doubled like as in Portrait.Reduced word-wise dithmatrix table to byte-wise table since the printhead is only 8 bits (pins) tall.  Fixed dithmatrix table accessing forits new format.  Saves space/cleaner code.The dither patterns have been redone with increased density.  Color andB/W patterns look much better in 320 mode; color patterns look muchbetter in 640 mode.  B/W/640 mode has dither beating problmes (screendithering is beating against print driver dithering), and the newpatterns are probably a bit too dark.  But all colors, and even subtleshades of different colors, look much truer.The Yellow/640 grayscale conversion bug, where the standard 640 lightyellow color comes out as white (ie, nothing) on paper, has been fixedby virtue of the denser dither patterns.  Exists in and must be fixedby some other means in the LQ driver (Test case: the "S" in Matt's"crystals" document won't show in B/W mode).A measure has been taken against 640-dithering beating against ourdithering in B/W mode (port/land) (limit dith tbl access in "bwP/Lpix").All told, the grayscale/color patterns look much better now.  The onlything that remains is perhaps a restructuring of the bits for some ofthe dither matrix entries so as to reduce 320-mode pattern artifacts.The RGB to KCMY conversion table is now built in memory rather thanbeing hardcoded and carried along so as to save abour 8K of disk space(Space Improvement #1).  Should be retrofitted to LQ driver.Command-period quit responsiveness has been improved somewhat (onedisadvantage of our run-length-encoding is the printer buffer filling,and that is what's mostly responsible for the slower-than-old-drivercommand-period response).  Also, IdleProc execution and network errorchecking is being done more frequently.  Needs to be retrofitted to LQdriver.Landscape speed improvement (Speed#8): superior "Lwht" white scanningalgorithm.  The qualifications are still the same (std white in stdctbl locations), but instead of an all-or-nothing whole-headscan-line-eliminate, it is now able to operate on parts of a headscan line.It may or may not be possible to successfully retrofit to LQ driver.White horizontal line banding if color vertical interlace on someImageWriterII's.  Fixed: instead of doing yellow, then yellow-interlace,then magenta, magenta interlace, etc., and backward 1/144" linefeedsbetween colors, we now do all 4 colors, forward 1/144", then all 4colors again.  Done for both portrait and landscape code.  Also savescode space, code looks better, and makes linefeeds smoother.ImageWriter I ID sequence (there *is* no sequence since the IW Ihas no self-ID command) is now recognized.  The old driver did the IDrequest only after PrJobDialog (from within PrPicFile), since it didn'tneed to dim color/sheet feeder buttons.  Therefore, there is a verylong delay when calling up PrJobDialog, due to one of several severelimitations of the PRINTER/MODEM direct-connect printer-port driverswhich need to be fixed.The ImageWriter I feature set does not include all of the ImageWriter IIfeatures, so a framework and code has been added to not try to use suchfeatures.  Before doing any draft/nondraft printing, the printer isasked for ID (ie, from within PrPicFile) so that we know which printeris connected.  This must be done because an application might callPrPicFile without first calling PrJobDialog (ie, Iduna).  Because ofthese code changes, printer error handling needs to be retested.D4		29-Mar-90All landscape modes are tentatively working.  Rigorous testing isvery necessary.  Unlike with portrait, 320/640 mode handling iscritical during vertical interlacing.Dither pattern handling need to be improved; landscape/interlace onlydraws patterns on one pass because of 640-dithering.Color patterns need to be improved; 640-mode double-pixel pairinterpretation of screen dither technique would be very nice to haveso that 640 colors would not look so muddy.When other bugs are finished, a speed improvement might be implementedfor the landcape modes.Source code has been projectorized so that it will appear on SystemDisk releases.D3		22-Mar-90On No-Gaps with Better, there would be unprinted whitespace areas.Fixed.  This was due to vertical imager-head-misalignment due to tworeasons: PrPicFile routine's band buffer allocation routines didvertical align-24 instead of align-16 and the Imager Portrait code's"onePband" was doing double "nextPline" even at last pin if interlacing.Landscape mode next release.D2		19-Mar-90		DevelopmentalNot-printing-in-color bug was a symptom of mechanical translation forthe very first (E0) release and has been fixed.Job Dialog From/To box interpretation has been improved.  All previouserror checking still exists, plus it's now possible to fill-in only onebox and have the results come out as expected.  For example, selecting"From: 5" and leaving "To:" blank will cause printing from 5..doclength.Likewise, one could fill in only "To: 8", leaving "From:" blank, forexample, thus causing only pages 1..8 to be printed.  Needs to beretrofitted to LQ driver.All portrait modes working: Faster+Standard, Better, || 50% reduction,|| 50% vertical condense.  This has involed the introduction of aninterlace technique in which every print head scan is done twice in somecases, because maximum vertical resolution on the ImageWriter must beachieved in this way.Boldface (only) is turned off during any interlace mode to compensatefor increased density.Final portrait mode anti-LQ sanitization: BW6 algorithm works again(13% gain for ~200 bytes code space); speed tests indicate about400% improvement over old IW driver in Better mode.  SCBs are supposedto track correctly but has not been tested.E1		9-Mar-90Official backing has been obtained for this project, to be finishedby April 1990.Obtained metrics print record hex dump for all cases with old IW driver,for compatiblity testing in the very near future.Note that, in general, the size of the driver will be decreasing as newreleases come out!Many preliminaries of converting the new LQ driver to the new IW driverhave been taken care of.  Among the highlights: First pass metrics:changed metrics scaling service routines from 3X to 2X.  Removed allLQ-specific code pertaining to sheet feeder and other things.  Removedbig paper sizes.  Eased bufdims allocation to 2X.  First pass of dialog/dialogdata/imager/metrics which describe fully the options specific towhat features the ImageWriter II imaging routine will/must have, suchas 50% reduction, single sheet feeder, etc.  Changed PAP NBP string.Changed all relevant user-interface strings.  Changed all relevant IDequates and ID service routines.  Changed all applicable documentation.The old IW driver always had boldface and unidirectional turned on.Since 1) we want to maintain a consistent default user interface withthe old driver, 2) it is awkward to have negative-logic check boxes inthe page setup dialog (such as "lighter" and "bidirectional"), and3) boldface/unidirectional options are orthogonal across all modes,there will be four Print Quality modes:	NAME:		PRINT METHOD:				ALGORITHM:		DEFAULT:	Text Mode	changes on the fly			text approx	Faster		non-boldface/bidirectional	graphics 1X	Standard	boldface/unidirectional		graphics 1X		default	Best		boldface/unidirectional		graphics 2XDialog boxes' art layout has been redone because items were removed.The run-length-encoding compression algorithm has been changed frombeing able to handle 8-pin as well as 24-pin models to being able tohandle 8-pin head fire model only, which is all that is needed here.Upon NewHandle error conditions, the real memory-full tool error($0201) is returned instead of the value given by the "e16.print"equate "memFullErr" ($FF80).  Has been retrofitted to LQ driver.For all 3 newcontrol2 dialog boxes, update events are now handled towork correctly with windoids such as Video Keyboard.  Has beenretrofitted to LQ driver.Next release (hopefully D2): fix color-not-working, first pass portrait,first pass Better mode/50% reduction.E0		21-Feb-90		ExperimentalStarted doing the brand-new ImageWriter driver as a "skunk_works"project on author's own time.  The purpose for doing this is that allthe benefits of the LQ driver will be inherited and will yield 2-3Xspeed improvements over the old driver.  See the README file, whichis almost identical across the two drivers.All of the initial, obvious name/date/etc changes have been made toboth the contents and comments of all the source files.  It is upand running.